# Put the interfaces in their zones (this changes traffic at once):
#   zone FWS_trust / interface ethernet0/1
#   zone FWS_untrust / interface ethernet0/0
#   zone FWS_dmz / interface ethernet0/2
#   zone FWS_lab / interface ethernet0/3
# Written inactive:
#   block-country: references 'blocked-country': address entry blocked-country: country XX, which the configuration does not resolve to addresses
#   lab-updates: host name object update-site: the form of an address object of a host name is not in the documentation FWShift could read
#   app-clients: schedule 'office-hours' is not converted; the rule would apply at all times; service app-ports: source ports, an ICMP code, SCTP ports or protocol 0, which a service object cannot say; host name object files.example.org: the form of an address object of a host name is not in the documen
#   p2p: not converted: application BitTorrent: application identification narrows the match
#   tunnels-to-partners: 'partners' holds members only its platform knows
#   to-branch-vpn: not converted: action tunnel vpn-to-branch: traffic of a VPN tunnel only
#   contractors-out: references 'wild-hosts': address entry wild-hosts: wildcard address '10.10.0.5 0.0.255.0'; source user match role contractors is not converted
